WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:12.000
Before October 7, you published the photo book "Life on the Border".  Which image from it means the most to you today, and why?

00:13.800 --> 00:23.533
There's a picture of five women, mothers, with their own children.

00:28.400 --> 00:30.166
Near the the border,

00:31.633 --> 00:33.700
they're taking them like this.

00:34.300 --> 00:36.500
The eyes

00:36.500 --> 00:39.866
of the children are (looking) inside the kibbutz

00:40.166 --> 00:45.066
and the mothers' looking to the border, to Gaza.

00:46.466 --> 00:50.300
I thought that it's an optimistic photo,

00:50.300 --> 00:54.366
because even though they know that there is Gaza ,

00:54.366 --> 00:58.233
they decided to grow up the children

00:58.233 --> 01:00.800
here in Kfar Aza, near the border.

01:02.400 --> 01:06.133
After October 7, something changed:

01:06.833 --> 01:09.866
Maybe they are looking over there just because

01:10.066 --> 01:11.566
they're afraid of them.

01:13.033 --> 01:14.333
Maybe...

01:17.000 --> 01:19.933
the children are looking inside the kibbutz,

01:21.400 --> 01:25.033
they know that in their generation,

01:25.033 --> 01:27.100
they will have to keep (preserve) it.

01:28.400 --> 01:30.266
And it's a little bit scary,

01:30.766 --> 01:33.166
and it's a little bit a change of mind.

01:35.233 --> 01:37.400
It's the most...

01:38.066 --> 01:40.466
it's the picture that I love more,

01:40.566 --> 01:46.800
more than all the 186 pictures in this book,

01:48.433 --> 01:52.766
but, I'm thinking in another way about it.

01:56.233 --> 01:58.233
So this is my book.
